## MVP 2 Backend Slice: OSM/Nominatim Geocoding + Direct Location Storage (2026-04-21)

### Scope Implemented

This change set implements a narrow backend-only MVP 2 slice for geocoding and coordinate storage on Ride and TripRequest create/update flows.

Implemented:
- Server-side Nominatim geocoding integration (OSM public search endpoint)
- Shared backend geocoding utility with deterministic query settings
- Schema/migration changes to store resolved addresses + coordinates directly on `rides` and `trip_requests`
- Ride and TripRequest create flow enforcement: both origin and destination must geocode successfully
- Ride and TripRequest edit flow updates: re-geocode only changed location fields
- Clear API error handling for missing/invalid input, no-result resolution, invalid coordinates, provider failure, and timeout
- Test updates with mocked geocoder behavior (no live external calls)

Explicitly not implemented in this slice:
- proximity filtering
- match suggestions
- route overlap
- autocomplete
- map rendering
- route geometry
- stop requests, negotiation, trust/completion features

---

### Files Changed

#### `src/lib/geocoding.ts` (NEW)

Added a shared backend geocoding utility used by Ride/TripRequest APIs.

Key behavior:
- Exposes `resolveLocationOrThrow(inputText)`
- Uses Nominatim Search API with deterministic params:
  - `format=jsonv2`
  - `limit=1`
  - `countrycodes=us`
  - `q=<trimmed-input>`
- Uses top result only (no ranking logic beyond first result)
- Validates and returns:
  - `inputText` (trimmed original)
  - `resolvedAddress` (`display_name` fallback to input)
  - `latitude`
  - `longitude`
- Validates coordinate ranges:
  - latitude `[-90, 90]`
  - longitude `[-180, 180]`
- Sends `User-Agent` header (`desti-mvp2-geocoder/1.0` with optional contact email)
- Includes optional `email` query param when `GEOCODER_CONTACT_EMAIL` is configured
- Supports timeout (`GEOCODER_TIMEOUT_MS = 8000`) via `AbortController`
- Throws typed `GeocodingError` codes:
  - `MISSING_INPUT`
  - `RESOLUTION_FAILED`
  - `INVALID_RESULT`
  - `PROVIDER_FAILURE`
  - `PROVIDER_TIMEOUT`
  - `SAME_COORDINATES`
- Adds `assertDistinctResolvedLocationsOrThrow` helper for origin/destination effective-coordinate equality checks.

Config handling in this module:
- `NOMINATIM_BASE_URL` optional, validated with URL parse, fallback to `https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org`
- `GEOCODER_CONTACT_EMAIL` optional, format-validated, ignored if invalid
- Config is server-only and not exposed to client-side code

#### `prisma/schema.prisma`

Added direct location storage fields to both models.

`Ride` additions:
- `originResolvedAddress String? @map("origin_resolved_address")`
- `originLatitude Float? @map("origin_latitude") @db.DoublePrecision`
- `originLongitude Float? @map("origin_longitude") @db.DoublePrecision`
- `destinationResolvedAddress String? @map("destination_resolved_address")`
- `destinationLatitude Float? @map("destination_latitude") @db.DoublePrecision`
- `destinationLongitude Float? @map("destination_longitude") @db.DoublePrecision`

`TripRequest` additions:
- `originResolvedAddress String? @map("origin_resolved_address")`
- `originLatitude Float? @map("origin_latitude") @db.DoublePrecision`
- `originLongitude Float? @map("origin_longitude") @db.DoublePrecision`
- `destinationResolvedAddress String? @map("destination_resolved_address")`
- `destinationLatitude Float? @map("destination_latitude") @db.DoublePrecision`
- `destinationLongitude Float? @map("destination_longitude") @db.DoublePrecision`

`originText`/`destinationText` already existed and remain required.

#### `prisma/migrations/20260421143000_add_geocoded_location_columns/migration.sql` (NEW)

Safe migration strategy implemented:
- Adds all six geocoded fields to `rides` as nullable columns
- Adds all six geocoded fields to `trip_requests` as nullable columns

Why nullable:
- Preserves compatibility for existing rows without backfill
- Avoids migration breakage on non-empty databases
- Runtime API now enforces required geocoding for new creates and changed location edits

